    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1999585111725994461",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlasg/status/1999585111725994461",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlasg/status/1999585111725994461",
      "text": "LASG ANNOUNCES TRAFFIC ADVISORY, DIVERSION PLAN FOR AJEGUNLE CITY YOUTH MARATHON\n\nThe Lagos State Government has announced a traffic diversion plan ahead of the Ajegunle City Youth Marathon, organised by the Society for Information and Human Advancement. The event is scheduled to hold on Saturday, 13th December, from 6:00 a.m.\n\nTo ensure the safety of participants and seamless traffic management, partial road closures will be implemented along the following routes:\n\nMaracana Stadium, Ojoku Street, Baale Road, Kirikiri Road, Wilmer Link Bridge, Okito Street, Kopariwo Street, Mba/Cardoso Street, Baale Road (Secretariat), Cemetery Street, Ojora Street, Baale Aiyetoro Street, Olowojeunjeje Street, Oduduwa Street, Layinka Street, Cemetery Road, Bakare Faro Street, Adejiyan Street, Ishaga Street, Onishapa Street, Itire Street, Ojo Road, and Signal Barracks (end point of the race).\n\nAll junctions and intersections along the corridor from Maracana Stadium to Signal Barracks, Ojo Road, will be temporarily closed and manned by LASTMA, the Nigeria Police Force (NPF), Federal Road Safety Corps (FRSC), and Lagos State Neighbourhood Corps (LSNC) to restrict access during the marathon.\n\nHowever, these junctions will be opened intermittently to allow controlled movement of other road users as the race progresses. Motorists are therefore advised to use the following alternative routes:\n\nAlternative Routes\n1. Traffic from Berger/Apapa–Oshodi Expressway heading to Olodi Apapa via Kirikiri should turn right into Industrial Road, link Idewu Street, proceed to Oluwa Street, connect Tolu Road, and link Baale Road to continue their journey.\n\n2. Traffic from Suru-Alaba (Lagos–Badagry Expressway) heading to Gaskiya Road and Iganmu Road will use a contra-flow on Cemetery Road from Techn oil turning to the roundabout to continue their movement.\n\n3. Traffic from Suru-Alaba (Lagos–Badagry Expressway) heading to Ojo Road should turn left before Signal Barracks into Charles Avenue, link Ligali Street, proceed to Evie Street, connect Abeje Street, and link Ojo Road.\n\nThe Lagos State Government assures that there will be minimal impact on traffic flow within the affected corridors.\nAdvisory: Motorists are urged to exercise patience and cooperate with traffic management officers, as the partial road closures are essential to ensuring a safe and successful marathon.\n\n@jidesanwoolu @drobafemihamzat @lagosMOT1 @gbenga_omo @gboyegaakosile @LanreBajulaiye @BarrBimbola @Mr_JAGs @Riddwane\n#AGreaterLagosRising \n#LASG",
