      "text": "S.R. 401 TRAFFIC ADVISORY FROM DEC. 12 THROUGH JAN. 2026:  The following advisory is from FDOT (Florida Department of Transportation)  Motorists are advised that a continuous closure will be implemented on the State Road (S.R. 401) western movable bridge from southbound S.R. 401 to westbound S.R. 528 beginning Friday, Dec. 12. The closure is expected to remain in place through January 2026.\n\nSouthbound S.R. 401 traffic wishing to travel to westbound S.R. 528 will be directed to the middle bridge on S.R. 401 and use the access road on the west side of S.R. 401 to exit to Westbound S.R. 528 Ramp.\n\nThe closure is necessary for the rehabilitation of the movable bridge, including replacing its protective paint layers and mechanical equipment. The other two bridges will remain open to accommodate both northbound and southbound traffic. Marine traffic may cause the bridges to close temporarily.\n\nThe work schedule is subject to change due to inclement weather or other unforeseen circumstances. For more details, please visit https://t.co/XPH21I1s5r\n\nFDOT encourages motorists to use caution, remain alert, and follow posted detour signs through the work zone.",
